4. Real-Life Example of KDD – Student Performance Prediction
Imagine a college wants to identify students who may fail their examinations.
KDD Step	College Example
Data Selection	Select marks and attendance
Data Cleaning	Remove incorrect records
Data Transformation	Convert marks into percentages
Data Mining	Find patterns related to failure
Evaluation	Check whether the patterns are reliable

Final knowledge: Students with low attendance and low internal marks may be at risk of failing.

The college can provide additional coaching to those students.
5. Difference Between KDD and Data Mining
This is a very important exam question.
KDD	Data Mining
Full form: Knowledge Discovery in Databases	Full form: Data Mining
Complete knowledge discovery process	One stage of KDD
Includes selection, cleaning, transformation, mining and evaluation	Focuses on discovering patterns
Produces useful knowledge	Produces patterns and relationships

Remember this:

KDD = Complete process

Data Mining = One important step in KDD

6. Advantages of KDD
1. Helps discover hidden patterns.
2. Supports better decision-making.
3. Helps predict future trends.
4. Improves business performance.
5. Converts large amounts of data into useful knowledge.
6. Helps identify relationships between different data items.
7. Pattern → Information → Knowledge
Example from machine maintenance:
- Pattern: Machine temperature increases before a machine failure.
- Information: High temperature is associated with machine problems.
- Knowledge: High temperature can be used as an early warning to predict possible machine failure.
